{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqqyd0ugp2b","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"daemon event loop wedge: synchronous git worktree add (distinct from the rerank spawn storm)","summary":"A SECOND, distinct root cause of the daemon \"wedge\" (GET /health times out, calls hang past socket timeout), complementary to the rerank spawn storm in [[note-mqqv4ix36dd]] (which is owned + already fixed under task 5 and is NOT re-fixed here). This vector: lib/git.js ran every git command via execFileSync on the daemon's single event-loop thread, so a worktree op froze ALL requests (including /health) for its whole duration. Measured on a 124-worktree repo: git worktree add ~5.5s, worktree remove ~2s, git status ~0.15s. An in-process event-loop probe showed 6.5-7.4s stalls 1:1 with each subconscious assignment prepare call (its createWorktree); the bench that reported the wedge (_fair_agentic_v2.py) interleaves a prepare before every search-context call, and its 3s /health timeout is shorter than the 5.5s git block, so it read the daemon as wedged. This path (prepare / branch_task / merge_attempt / merge_feature / automode judge-merge) hits the synchronous git on EVERY task dispatch,\n\n[Long raw evidence preserved as structured source chunks.]","category":null,"tags":["daemon","git","event-loop","performance","worktree","wedge","search-context"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T18:03:05.992Z","vec":[-0.07866210490465164,-0.009561000391840935,0.014668143354356289,0.05252835527062416,0.04608626663684845,-0.11949196457862854,-0.02467082440853119,0.037809960544109344,0.07278212159872055,0.019050177186727524,-0.03259938955307007,0.017479272559285164,0.0067481379956007,-0.03718014061450958,-0.011026209220290184,-0.04332788288593292,0.008083978667855263,-0.002517340937629342,-0.026185492053627968,0.00038847129326313734,-0.042043864727020264,0.04922665283083916,-0.0016891664126887918,0.04400677978992462,0.02731606923043728,-0.051092084497213364,-0.11541342735290527,-0.05803295